  "items": [
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3n22xdtz4kk2i",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "People who have no contact with coders seem to have no idea how much an entire profession transformed in less than a year due to AI. It is so weird to still see comments here that AI hasn’t changed anything or that AI code is bad or that companies are retreating from AI use. Does not match reality.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3n22xdtz4kk2i",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-11T22:00:44.261Z",
      "likes": 512,
      "replies": 30,
      "reposts": 66,
      "score": 8.2,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.8,
        "recency": 0.9,
        "age_hours": 24.6
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3n22xsngwis2i",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "This is not an argument that AI is all good or a hype post that you should learn AI today or fall behind. I think there is a limited time to engage with this transition and decide how to use AI in ways that make professions work better and center humans. Ignoring reality will not get us there.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3n22xsngwis2i",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-11T22:09:00.695Z",
      "likes": 151,
      "replies": 6,
      "reposts": 9,
      "score": 7,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.2,
        "recency": 0.9,
        "age_hours": 24.5
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3n22xifmn2c2i",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "Even I, who has been talking about AI for a long time, has been surprised at how fast things have altered fundamentally in the real world for a major profession. Adoption and transformation usually takes a longer time (It will, of course, not just be coding that AI changes. )",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3n22xifmn2c2i",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-11T22:03:16.949Z",
      "likes": 135,
      "replies": 2,
      "reposts": 3,
      "score": 6.9,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.2,
        "recency": 0.9,
        "age_hours": 24.6
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:ckaz32jwl6t2cno6fmuw2nhn/app.bsky.feed.post/3n25i2e2yi22m",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "Researcher Will Depue discovered that 4 top Chinese labs’ models were all trained on Blackwell GPUs (GB200 & GB300), which are fully restricted from sale to China\n\nhis method is purely forensic, no insider information was used\n\nunemploymentlabs.com/checkpoint-f...",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3n25i2e2yi22m",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-12T22:04:58.647Z",
      "likes": 35,
      "replies": 2,
      "reposts": 7,
      "score": 6.3,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.7,
        "recency": 1,
        "age_hours": 0.5
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3n24xvcnir22i",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "oh I see why some people are predicting financial doom regarding Jensen's departure from NVIDIA. The new CEO, Colette Kress, was the CFO and has been opposed to circular financing deals. No more questionable free rides for datacenters and hyperscalers (that will make the AI grifters sad).",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3n24xvcnir22i",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-12T17:15:49.517Z",
      "likes": 21,
      "replies": 2,
      "reposts": 2,
      "score": 5.8,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.4,
        "recency": 1,
        "age_hours": 5.4
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3n24xvcnsjk2i",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "I don't think this pops the bubble. I think it slows the bubble's inflation. Counterintuitively, slowing the bubble's inflation could increase the odds that the AI market settles into a steady state or has a soft landing if the bubble pops.\n\n(I am not an economist)",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3n24xvcnsjk2i",
